  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on whether a lottery includes a sure (certain) outcome, which is absent in both lotteries. The individual, however, bases their reasoning on the relative probabilities of winning a non-zero amount, explicitly favoring the higher chance of winning. There is no mention or implication that the individual considered whether an outcome was certain (i.e., 100% probability). The information considered by the individual (probabilities of non-zero outcomes) is different from the information required by the decision reason (presence of a sure outcome). Furthermore, the justification (higher chance to win) does not align with the rule of the decision reason (prefer lottery without a sure outcome). Since the decision reason would not discriminate between these two lotteries (neither has a sure outcome), and the individual’s reasoning follows a different logic entirely, it is unlikely the reason was used. Therefore, the match is very weak.",
